  "title": "China's Shenzhou-24 Space Mission with First Pakistani Astronaut",
  "summary": "China launched its Shenzhou-24 crewed mission to bring three astronauts to Tiangong space station, including Pakistan's Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, marking the first foreign national to participate in China's crewed space program. Ali will return to Earth aboard the Shenzhou-23 spacecraft after spending a week in orbit.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "China launched its Shenzhou-24 crewed spaceship carrying three astronauts, including Pakistan's Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, the first foreign national to participate in the country's crewed space programme.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The spacecraft, atop a Long March-2F carrier rocket, blasted off from the Jiuquan Satellite Launch Centre in northwest China, with officials declaring the launch successful minutes later.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ali will return to Earth aboard the Shenzhou-23 spacecraft after spending about a week in orbit, while Chinese astronauts typically stay at the station for about six months.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
