      "title": "China launches crewed mission with first Pakistani astronaut aboard",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/china-launches-crewed-mission-with-first-pakistani-astronaut-aboard-126112500064_1.html",
      "description": "China on Wednesday launched its Shenzhou-24 crewed spaceship carrying three astronauts, including Pakistan's Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, the first foreign national to participate in the country's crewed space programme.\nThe spaceship, atop a Long March-2F carrier rocket, blasted off from the Jiuquan Satellite Launch Centre in northwest China, with officials declaring the launch successful minutes later.\nThe crew comprises mission commander and spacecraft pilot Tang Hongbo, flight engineer Wu Yi and Ali, who will become the first foreign astronaut to visit China's orbiting Tiangong space station.\nAli will return to Earth aboard the Shenzhou-23 spacecraft after spending about a week in orbit, while Chinese astronauts typically stay at the station for about six months.\nThe spacecraft is expected to dock with the Tiangong space station in about three hours.\nChina built its own space station after it was reportedly excluded from the International Space Station (ISS) over concerns about the .",
